+# Minimal V2 repair notes
+
+V1 remains sealed and unchanged. This successor addresses source audit S1–S3 only; root focused repair review is pending before publication or execution.
+
+- S1: Copy each native fresh VALID dictionary and alias saved `served_micro_F1`/`served_macro_F1` to the analysis names. All original fields and five native results remain. No prediction reconstruction or new metric formula.
+- S2: Before Torch imports, array loads or comparisons, validate complete original shared/reference entries, declared/completed 18/24 counts, six reference groups, exact source/entry seals and entry SHA, original release SHA, frozen study/pairs/methods and chosen entry/family output identities. Cross-link observed launch release SHA, argv and pinned owner source to those originals; link native launch/release/cohort and the shared adoption pointers to the chosen cohorts. Preserve bound owner reports/inclusive cost context and available declared cell inventory on failure. Reuse that early bound cost object in the unchanged analysis. Existing inclusive wall/RSS caps remain enforced; nested costs are not summed.
+- S3: Use resident original files within `HERE.parent`. Replace the transfer flag with original-location digest verification before readout. Bind all 29 original selected checkpoints and stream their SHA checks without loading weights before Torch. Checkpoints/data/predictions/diagnostic/comparison PT files remain on the allocation; transfer only small JSON/CSV/Markdown reports to Mac.
+
+## Inactive contract additions
+
+`RELEASE.disabled.json` adds original `reference_fit_release`, `native_fit_release`, `artifact_mode=resident_original_files`, and `transfer_scope=small_analysis_reports_only`. Origin inventory V2 adds the same resident mode, `selected_checkpoint_digests_verified_at_original_locations_before_readout`, and `selected_checkpoints` mapping each existing `selected_origins` cell/seed key to exact path/bytes/SHA. Approval fields and file bindings remain false/null/empty.
+
+New small execution reports: `OWNER_ENTRY_CONTEXT.json` and `CHECKPOINT_ORIGIN_VERIFICATION.json`. The original scientific tables and decisions are unchanged.
+
+## Verification and preserved scope
+
+Only Python/JSON parse checks, exact source/provenance hashes, AST ordering/alias/safe-load checks and the inactive default invocation were run. They passed. Every V1 manifest file was reverified. `analysis.py` is byte-identical to V1 (SHA `07be5b87f903a2a702c10a57ffe9865a0887865280ef4454326750f9c5e8d61b`).
+
+No scientific outcome, actual receipt, dataset, label, prediction, checkpoint or array was opened during preparation. No provider/model/fit/replay/forward/server/GPU/monitor/scheduler execution or numerical/parity test occurred. Frozen formulas, thresholds, serving, source fits, seeds and three-pair uncertainty remain unchanged. This source packet establishes no completion/custody/quality verdict.
+
+`REPAIR_PROVENANCE.json` binds the audited V1 identities and the audit; `REPAIR_DIFF.patch` records the source/contract changes. `SOURCE_BINDINGS.json` adds those small source-only provenance files and original owner launcher sources, which must accompany resident publication.
